{% extends '@CitadelAureum/core/docs/layout.html.twig' %}

{% block article %}
    <p>
        Lost property registers items found in the hotel and tracks them until
        they're back with their owner, or responsibly disposed of.
    </p>

    <h2>How an item moves</h2>
    <p>
        A found item starts <strong>open</strong>. Once stored, mark it
        <strong>stored</strong>. When the owner is identified it becomes
        <strong>waiting for collection</strong> or <strong>waiting to be
        posted</strong>, and finally <strong>collected</strong> or
        <strong>posted</strong>. Unclaimed items end as
        <strong>disposed</strong>. Each change is recorded in the item's log.
    </p>

    <h2>Common tasks</h2>
    <ol class="au-docs-steps">
        <li>Open <strong>General → Lost Property</strong> and register the item with where and when it was found.</li>
        <li>Describe the item well. A good description is how a phone call from a guest gets matched to a shelf in the store room.</li>
        <li>With manage permission, update the status as the item moves, so the register always matches the shelf.</li>
    </ol>
{% endblock %}
